Z||000006||Shaun41178||02-17-2000||10:36 PM||||i don't want to sound like a braggert but I think I have one of the fastest or the fastest Fiero of the Fiero owners on this board.  I have a best 0-60 time of 5.6 (G-Tech) and have run a best qtr mile time of 14.1 at a meagerly 90 mph(actual qtr mile track).  1/8th mile time is consistently around or under 9 seconds with a best of 8.8.  Faster then many stock and  modified f-bodies of the 4th generation and newer model Cobras.  This is also with an auto tranny.  Of course my car is not stock to run these times.  Main power adder is nitrous.  I have surprised many cars out on the streets and have posted all the kills here in the forum.  AS far as exotic or unusual; its pretty plain as far as the body goes.  Sleeper I guess you could say||||reg||6
Z||000007||cobra427||02-17-2000||10:54 PM||||Phil,  are you the Phil Hardin that was listed in the March issue of Hot Rod mag under East Coast Long Haul Gang? Or maybe the Philip Randolf?  That must have been quite a trip?||||reg||1
Z||000008||BBBAD GT||02-17-2000||11:39 PM||||I've gone 11.13 @ 127 mph......in my Blown 89 Stang  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But seriously, I don't think we buy Fieros for the dragstrip, but for other reasons we all know.  I've found out the amount of money you have to spend just to keep up with the low 13 sec stockers of today is just too much. It boils down to the cost/benifit relationship.  <P>But, you can bet on me getting some ET's on my 87 GT as soon as it gets warm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/</A>  ||||reg||12
Z||000009||Oreif||02-17-2000||11:43 PM||||There are 2 rules for "the Fastest"<BR>1. Someone is always faster.<BR>2. Speed is just a question of money....<BR>   How fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
