Z||000012||BBBAD GT||02-18-2000||02:27 PM||||I'm not flaming or anything, but I know a C5 can do the 1/4 mi in low low 13's and usually high 12's with a good driver at 110 mph.  ET's are a function of traction most of the time, and MPH is a function of how much HP you are putting down according to weight.  I've driven a 6sp C5 before, and came away really impressed.  <P>Now, if you stuff a V8 in a Fiero, can most likely eat that C5 for breakfast if its built right.<P>||||reg||1
