Z||000017||87PegasusGT||02-21-2000||04:30 PM||||In answer to the DOHC question,<BR>Dennis Lagrua's turbo 2.8 pulling 200hp is claiming 0-60 in 5.6 seconds. My 3.4 is ported and built to 220 after all mods but after my T3 install, I am hoping for 300hp or better. That SHOULD put me faster than a new Vette and still have good road manners and decent gas mileage while retaining stock appearance and weight.||||reg||1
Z||000018||william_thorniii||02-21-2000||06:40 PM||||87,<P>One thing to remember is that 300 bhp on a turbo is not directly comparable to 300 bhp on a naturally aspirated engine.  It is somewhat like comparing the clock speeds from a PI to a PII (If you are into computers).  From what I understand this is due to the fact that turbocharged engines do not reach their peak power as quickly as push rod engines of the same rating due to lag.  Of course this can be minimalized, but I just wanted to throw that out.  <P>Eddie,<P>A better comparison would be to MWS (fiero-list).  He has a 96 DOHC 3.4L in his Fiero.  I know that he has posted some preliminary #'s, but was still working the bugs out at the time.  Also the 96+ DOHC's have a much larger TB and intake and therefore breathe better on the top end.  So it is not still a direct comparision although they are rated the same in power. <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
